      "message": "We should make this clearer to indicate what the bug is:\n\n\n```\nThe underlying issue is that both `shmalloc` and `malloc/free` are\nboth set up to use the same memory region for allocation. If they\nare both enabled, they will overwrite each other.\n\nThe change in https://crrev.com/c/5166769 triggered this behavior\nsince it makes `CONFIG_MALLOC` take effect when \n`USE_BUILTIN_STDLIB` is `0`. \n```",
